  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 809.01 Applicability",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 809.01 Applicability.\n\n(a) This part shall apply to any person who:\n\n(1) Generates or collects spent lead-acid batteries destined for reclamation;\n\n(2) Transports spent lead-acid batteries destined for reclamation;\n\n(3) Reclaims spent lead-acid batteries; or\n\n(4) Exports or imports spent lead-acid batteries for reclamation.\n\n(b) The reclamation of spent lead-acid batteries through regeneration, such as by electrolyte replacement, shall be subject to Env-Hw 400 and Env-Hw 502, but shall not otherwise be subject to the hazardous waste rules.\n\nSource. #5053, eff 1-24-91; ss by #5886, eff 8-26-94; ss by #7333, eff 8-1-00; ss by #7578, eff 10-13-01; ss by #9367, eff 1-28-09; ss by #12350, eff 8-14-17; ss by #12922, eff 11-23-19; ss by #14526, eff 2-28-26, EXPIRES: 2-28-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw800.html"
